From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Allow importing on linux riscv64

lib3mf/__init__.py raises OSError for any Linux machine type other than
x86_64 and aarch64, before Lib3MF.py ever tries to load lib3mf.so. The
library itself is built from source for the host architecture, so the
allowlist is the only thing that stops a riscv64 wheel from importing.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; python-wheels does not open issues/PRs on third-party repos]
---
 py_lib3mf/__init__.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/py_lib3mf/__init__.py b/py_lib3mf/__init__.py
index 062a6e8..69040ed 100644
--- a/py_lib3mf/__init__.py
+++ b/py_lib3mf/__init__.py
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ if system not in ("linux", "darwin", "windows", "emscripten"):
 
 # Relax machine checks to include aarch64/arm64 and wasm
 if system == "linux":
-    if machine not in ("x86_64", "aarch64", "arm64"):
+    if machine not in ("x86_64", "aarch64", "arm64", "riscv64"):
         raise OSError(f"Unsupported Machine Type: {machine}")
 elif system == "windows":
     if machine not in ("x86_64", "amd64"):
